it might be the middle of January but  there were still a few Game of the Year  awards to hand out from last year the  academy of interactive arts and sciences  has revealed its nominees for the best  games of 2015 rise the tomb raider and  the witcher 3 wild hunt are at the top  of the pile with eight nominations each  tomb raider and witcher 3 are nominated  for overall game of the year of course  but blood-borne fallout 4 and ori and  the blind forest are also up for the big  prize plenty of other games have  received multiple nominations too  including star wars battlefront and  batman arkham knight we have the full  list of nominees at gamespot the dice  awards will be held in las vegas on  thursday febuary 18th with returning  host Pete Holmes Metal Gear creator  Hideo Kojima will be inducted into the  Hall of Fame and former nintendo  president satoru Otto will be honored  with a posthumous Lifetime Achievement  Award 2016 is shaping up to be a big  year for gaming it's always nice to look  back you can still check out our game of  the year coverage at gamespot.com / game  of the year and for all the video game  news you need in the new year you'll  already be in the right place
 

